A||||8||fiero56||Fiero Factory Swap Meet||||10||
Z||000000||fiero56||04-30-2000||10:56 PM||||The swap meet down in Toney Alabama was awsome! Weather was perfect(70s-80s) sunny, no clouds, just had a very brief sprinkle of rain Saturday afternoon. Got to see "The Man" Ed Parks again, toured the Fiero Factory and parts yard, met the Fiero Factory workers and talked with them for awhile. There were quite a few vendors there, but maybe not even half what I would have expected(maybe 12-15). Rodney was there with great stuff, just not enough, there were several items I wanted to purchase that he was sold out of. Ended up getting some great deals from a fellow forum member, mrfiero(actually every dollar I spent was at his stand). Met several other PFF members, got to see/hear/watch a Northstar Fiero, got to look at and listen to a serious quad4 Fiero. Plus many other beautifull Fieros showed up. I plan to attend next year if Ed sponsors another. I also got to the see the new "Fiero Factory" sign.<P>More to come, I just got home a little over an hour ago. William, I have both black stickers, and you have both white stickers. Need to trade sometime.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 04-30-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||william_thorniii||04-30-2000||11:10 PM||||DOH!<P>How did you have time to post this and edit it before I just could post my original... I guess I am just toooooooooo oooooooo oooooooo oooooooo ooooooooo long winded.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I can't believe you stole my black sticker :P<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||2
Z||000002||fiero56||05-01-2000||03:09 PM||||Maybe it's beacuase I'm a faster typer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">.<P>It was a 1200 mile round trip, but was definitly worth it. Got to watch an '87GT get disasembled(somone made the comment it looked like it blew up, with door panels laying on the ground). Met some great people, and visited with others that I knew from previous meetings. I even got to sign "the wall"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, and saw Ed's "Fiero Wall of Shame." There are some very interesting pieces on that wall. Plus, I saw a fiero convertible. I met several other PFF members, but couldn't find the member with the red Xterra??? there. There was a PFF banner in the back window. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-01-2000||04:16 PM||||Jeez, Guys. What a weekend! Didn't get home until 2:30 this morning. Helped Jason and Jazz get the motor out of the "parts GT". Learned a lot (never pulled a cradle, before). Met a bunch of great folks... William, 56, Mike Hill, and all the others whose names escape me due to the lack of shut-eye. Saw some really interesting rides. (Words can't describe the sound of that Northstar installation. Gawd.) Got a 3.4 demo ride. (Want one, real bad.) And drank *most of* the biggest freaking Margarita I've ever seen. <BR>Thanks to Ed Parks and Rosy, and all the other folks who made this whole thing possible. <BR>Ed was counting registration slips yesterday. Seems like I remember hearing "150+(?) people from 25 different states." Amazing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||05-01-2000||04:32 PM||||Raydar,<P>Can you share any specifics about the difference in the 3.4 from the 2.8? I've got a 3.4 long block onmy garage floor and am contemplating starting a rebuild so it will be ready for my next car(when I buy another one). Did the 3.4 have: a performance cam; aftermarket headers; auto or stick; etc?<P>Roy L.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||05-01-2000||04:47 PM||||I didn't actually drive the car. I was a bit too "happy", at the time (due to the previously mentioned margarita). Wouldn't have taken the chance. <BR>But... The 3.4 that I rode in was an automatic. Wanted to know what to expect, since mine is an automatic, as well. The guy that owned the car (having a brain-cramp, and can't remember his name) said that he figured it made about 180 HP. From what I've heard about the swap, that sounds about right for an un-modded 3.4. <BR>But it was *damned* quick. <BR>As for the differences between the 2.8 and the 3.4 (You need the Camaro/Firebird version), the biggest difference is the starter location. (Transaxle is in the way. Has to be moved.) Check the Fiero Factory page for the rest of the mods. I'll try to post the link, later. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||05-01-2000||04:52 PM||||Hey Fiero56,<BR>I was the one with the red Xterra. I was picking up my new 3.4 which Ed had prepare for me :-). Too bad I didn't meet you. It was great there. I met Rydar and Paul. Sure I missed others. I stayed only about 3 hrs. Also bought other parts from Ed and Rodney. Definetely a Fiero owners heaven. All those cars for parts!!! Plus the nice owners rides. The Northstar sound in a Fiero... WOW!!! Awesome!!<BR>My 3.4 came ready with the required brackets for my application (88 Formula), fittings for the oil preasure switch, balancer and all gaskets required. Looks so beautiful all clean and new!! I just need to receive my new headers to start with the install. Hope by end of May have it running....||||reg||1
Z||000007||PAUL88GT||05-01-2000||06:28 PM||||I enjoyed meeting a few other forum members (Raydar, Database Nut, Alex4mula). I was suprised by the number of people who had not heard of the forum. We need to get the word our better or a few people need to get "connected."<P>It was my first swap meet. I was a little disappointed in the total number of vendors or participant with parts for sale or trade. I did not find the passenger side GT tailight I needed. I guess I have to order the lens from Chriswell or get it on E-bay.<P>I did enjoy seeing all the GTs, Formulas, and two awesome kit cars and meeting a lot of new people. I agree an enjoyable part of the meet was watching people dissemble that GT. A fellow Huntsvillian is going to build a trailor out of the rear end of that vehicle to pull behind his White 88GT.<P>The Orange Formula with the new paint was exceptional.  See you next year.<P>Paul ||||reg||1
Z||000008||85gt||05-01-2000||06:52 PM||||I just didn't get to stay long enough. My wife fell in love with the purpleish colored fiero for sale. Might get her one for her birthday. I got a shifter console that I've been needing. I sure liked the orange formula, it was sweet. Didn't have a chance to talk to too many people, and I'm terrible at names. I was wearing the purple LSU hat if anyone spotted me. Can't wait till next year. <P>Matt<p>[This message has been edited by 85gt (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||6
